  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A guide sheet lists room highlights and approximate viewing times without requiring a fixed order.\", \"decision\": \"How should a visitor with little time plan a visit?\", \"goal\": \"Help visitors find a satisfying route through the museum while keeping reception and volunteers manageable.\", \"problem\": \"A volunteer-run local museum wants to make a weekend visit easier to navigate. It has a modest collection, printed guides, a reception table, flexible volunteer positions, and several rooms that can remain open independently. The decisions concern interpretation and visitor organization, not conservation rules or safety policy.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVisitors state their available time, and reception selects fitting highlights from the guide sheet. The suggested visit begins with the time limit.\nReception offers several highlight bundles with viewing times, and visitors choose a bundle. Time and content can be compared together.\nVisitors select highlights from the guide sheet, and reception helps trim them to the available time. The suggested visit begins with the visitor’s interests."
    }
